<%- include('partials/head') %>
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-text">
  <h1>See a UHS doctor without the queue</h1>
  <p>
    The University Health Service telemedicine platform lets students, staff and their dependants book
    appointments online, consult a doctor by video or audio call, and keep their medical records safe and
    easy to find.
  </p>
  <div class="row">
    <a class="btn btn-light" href="/register">Create a patient account</a>
    <a class="btn btn-accent" href="/login">Sign in</a>
  </div>
  </div>
  <img class="hero-logo" src="/static/img/ui-logo.png" alt="University of Ibadan" width="600" height="200">
</section>

<div class="grid grid-3">
  <div class="card feature">
    <h3>Book online</h3>
    <p>Pick a date and a free time slot that suits you. No phone calls, no waiting to be attended to just to book.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card feature">
    <h3>Consult remotely</h3>
    <p>Suitable cases can be handled by secure video or audio call, saving you an unnecessary trip to the clinic.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card feature">
    <h3>Electronic records</h3>
    <p>Your consultations, prescriptions and history are kept in one secure electronic file — no more missing folders.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card feature">
    <h3>Reminders</h3>
    <p>Get reminders before your appointment and on your follow-up date, in the app and by email.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card feature">
    <h3>Message your doctor</h3>
    <p>Follow-up questions? Send a secure message to the doctor who saw you.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card feature">
    <h3>Already have a UHS folder?</h3>
    <p>Visit the records office with your ID card and they will link your existing record to an online account.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="alert alert-warn">
  <strong>Emergencies:</strong> telemedicine is not for emergencies. If you have severe chest pain, difficulty breathing,
  heavy bleeding, loss of consciousness or another emergency, go to the UHS emergency unit immediately.
</div>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
